From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BuiltInPackages: opt out of upstream mikkelsen via LY_USE_SYSTEM_MIKKELSEN

Stage 1 of the Fedora-inclusion roadmap (BUNDLED_LIBRARIES.md) migrates
each `ly_associate_package` entry that has a clean Fedora equivalent
from the upstream packages.o3de.org CDN to the system package. mikkelsen
is the smallest, lowest-risk first migration: it's a single
self-contained C file (MikkTSpace tangent-space generator), MIT-like
license, already packaged as `mikkelsen` + `mikkelsen-devel` in
hellaenergy/o3de-dependencies on COPR.

This patch wraps the mikkelsen entry in an opt-in cmake gate so the
upstream behavior is preserved by default. Setting
`-DLY_USE_SYSTEM_MIKKELSEN=ON` (which the o3de-rpm spec does in %build
when the `system_mikkelsen` bcond is enabled) skips the upstream
fetcher and instead calls `find_package(mikkelsen REQUIRED)`, which
cmake resolves against our companion sources/Findmikkelsen-system.cmake
(installed into cmake/3rdParty/ during %prep — that directory is on
CMAKE_MODULE_PATH, see cmake/3rdParty.cmake:435). The find module
locates the system mikktspace headers and library and creates the
`3rdParty::mikkelsen` INTERFACE target that engine code expects.

The else-branch is load-bearing: gating out `ly_associate_package`
without replacing it means nothing ever triggers `find_package`, the
target never gets created, and consumers silently link nothing.
Discovered the hard way on build 10418378 — the binary RPM correctly
declared `Requires: mikkelsen` but no engine .so actually linked to
libmikktspace, caught by the Tier 2 swap-consistency test.

The pattern is intentional: each Stage 1 package gets its own
`LY_USE_SYSTEM_<PACKAGE>` gate (with a matching else-branch find_package
call), so packagers can migrate one bundle at a time without touching
the others.

---
 cmake/3rdParty/Platform/Linux/BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/cmake/3rdParty/Platform/Linux/BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake
+++ b/cmake/3rdParty/Platform/Linux/BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake
@@ -24,7 +24,11 @@
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME freetype-2.11.1-rev1-linux                        TARGETS Freetype                    PACKAGE_HASH 28bbb850590507eff85154604787881ead6780e6eeee9e71ed09cd1d48d85983)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME Lua-5.4.4-rev1-linux                              TARGETS Lua                         PACKAGE_HASH d582362c3ef90e1ef175a874abda2265839ffc2e40778fa293f10b443b4697ac)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME mcpp-2.7.2_az.2-rev1-linux                        TARGETS mcpp                        PACKAGE_HASH df7a998d0bc3fedf44b5bdebaf69ddad6033355b71a590e8642445ec77bc6c41)
+if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_MIKKELSEN)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME mikkelsen-1.0.0.4-linux                           TARGETS mikkelsen                   PACKAGE_HASH 5973b1e71a64633588eecdb5b5c06ca0081f7be97230f6ef64365cbda315b9c8)
+else()
+    find_package(mikkelsen REQUIRED)
+endif()
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME googlebenchmark-1.7.0-rev1-linux                  TARGETS GoogleBenchmark             PACKAGE_HASH 230e1881e31490820f0bd2059df4741455b52809ac73367e278e1e821ac89c9b)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME qt-5.15.2-rev9-linux                              TARGETS Qt                          PACKAGE_HASH db4bcd2003262f4d8c7d7da832758824fc24e53da5895edef743f67a64a5c734)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME png-1.6.37-rev2-linux                             TARGETS PNG                         PACKAGE_HASH 5c82945a1648905a5c4c5cee30dfb53a01618da1bf58d489610636c7ade5adf5)
